│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ butterfly_phase_mixer                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This ansatz uses a parameter-efficient butterfly topology rather than the seed’s          │
│                          │ nearest-neighbor CZ line. Independent RY rotations first select a measurement basis for   │
│                          │ each qubit, while four shared RZ parameters provide regularized phase corrections across  │
│                          │ paired wires. Two complementary CNOT matchings then propagate pairwise phase information  │
│                          │ globally in only two entangling stages. Parametrized CRY gates between the stages add     │
│                          │ controlled, noncommuting mixing, and a final independent RY layer converts the resulting  │
│                          │ phase correlations into the Z populations used by the fixed readout.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The design uses 20 trainable parameters per block: enough local freedom to distinguish    │
│                          │ feature-pair roles, but substantially constrained phase and controlled-mixing parameters  │
│                          │ to reduce overfitting. The alternating long-range matchings also align naturally with the │
│                          │ complete set of 28 two-qubit feature couplings without reproducing the seed’s             │
│                          │ linear-entanglement approach.                                                             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0529                                                                                   │
