│ patch_description        │ Replace the final RZ layer with RY rotations while retaining the same parameter count.    │
│                          │ Final RZ gates commute with Z measurement, so the last block’s eight post-rotation        │
│                          │ parameters have no effect on predictions and receive zero gradients; analogous gates in   │
│                          │ earlier blocks also provide only indirect utility. Final RY gates directly rotate phase   │
│                          │ and correlation information into measurable Z populations, improve gradient flow, and     │
│                          │ give every parameter copy an observable role. This should improve loss and convergence    │
│                          │ without increasing circuit size or reducing parameter efficiency.                         │
