│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ euler_local_line                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the two-axis local layers and ineffective post-entangler RZ layer with            │
│                          │ independent RZ–RY–RZ Euler rotations on every qubit, while reverting the entangler        │
│                          │ topology from the underperforming ring to the better-generalizing open CZ line. This      │
│                          │ preserves exactly 24 parameters per block (146 total), adds full local SU(2) expressivity │
│                          │ around successive uploads and repeated blocks, and removes the closing CZ edge associated │
│                          │ with increased depth, validation loss, and generalization gap. Unlike the current final   │
│                          │ RZ gates, which commute with Z readout and the diagonal feature encoding, the Euler layer │
│                          │ includes RY rotations that convert learned phase information into measurable populations. │
