│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ close_cz_ring                                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Close the brickwork CZ chain with a [7, 0] coupling. This gives every qubit degree two    │
│                          │ and removes the representational asymmetry of the endpoint qubits, which is especially    │
│                          │ relevant because all eight Z expectations contribute equally to the fixed mean readout.   │
│                          │ The added gate is parameter-free and is disjoint from [1, 2], [3, 4], and [5, 6], so it   │
│                          │ completes the second parallel entangling layer without increasing the ideal circuit depth │
│                          │ or parameter count. This should improve global feature mixing while preserving the        │
│                          │ current ansatz's parameter efficiency and fast convergence.                               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
