│ patch_name               │ adaptive_central_crz                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the fixed middle CZ with a trainable CRZ so the circuit can learn the strength    │
│                          │ and sign of the central coupling rather than imposing maximal entanglement. Restore the   │
│                          │ empirically stronger post-entanglement RY basis-mixing layer, while removing the post-RY  │
│                          │ on wire 3 to offset the new CRZ parameter. This keeps 24 parameters per block and 146     │
│                          │ total parameters, improves parameter efficiency relative to simply adding capacity, and   │
│                          │ reduces the gate count by one per block. The near-zero CRZ initialization also starts as  │
│                          │ a weak coupling, which should support faster, more stable optimization and reduce         │
│                          │ overfitting.                                                                              │
