│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ skip_chain_cz                                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current candidate uses 24 trainable parameters per block (146 total), Adam with       │
│                          │ learning rate 0.03, batches of 15, 30 steps per epoch, validation-loss selection, and     │
│                          │ patience 75. Its asymmetric omission of the post-RY gate on qubit 3 and the isolated      │
│                          │ trainable CRZ increase overfitting: train accuracy reaches 0.97 while test accuracy falls │
│                          │ to 0.84.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new block restores a complete post-RY layer and removes the CRZ bottleneck. It        │
│                          │ replaces the nearest-neighbor CZ line with a connected next-nearest-neighbor schedule:    │
│                          │ two skip chains are coupled by the final 6–7 edge. This allows phase-map information to   │
│                          │ move between less-local qubits while retaining seven fixed entanglers and the same 24     │
│                          │ parameters per block. Fixed CZ gates avoid adding parameter variance, while balanced      │
│                          │ rotations on every measured qubit should reduce the train-test gap and recover the        │
│                          │ stronger validation/test behavior of the prior symmetric blocks.                          │
