│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ paired_sharing_adaptive_bridge                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Exploit the permutation-like structure induced by all-pairs binary feature encoding and   │
│                          │ the symmetric mean-Z readout by sharing rotation parameters across paired wires. This     │
│                          │ reduces each block from 24 to 13 unique parameters and the full model from 146 to 80      │
│                          │ parameters, improving regularization and parameter efficiency while preserving            │
│                          │ independent copies across the six fixed blocks. Replace the redundant duplicated CZ(7,0), │
│                          │ whose two consecutive applications cancel exactly, with the previously stronger           │
│                          │ skip-chain topology. Add one trainable CRZ on the bridge between the even and odd skip    │
│                          │ chains, allowing Adam to adapt the inter-chain phase correlation without allocating       │
│                          │ separate parameters to every entangler.                                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.1548                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
