│ patch_description        │ This block uses independent RY rotations to convert the diagonal IsingZZ feature phases   │
│                          │ into measurable population differences, followed by a Möbius-ladder CZ network. The       │
│                          │ topology combines an eight-qubit ring with four opposite-qubit links, providing short-    │
│                          │ and long-range mixing without trainable entanglers. A final independent RY layer performs │
│                          │ local readout adaptation. Using only 16 parameters per block improves parameter           │
│                          │ efficiency and limits overfitting while retaining qubit-specific expressivity.            │
