│ patch_name               │ symmetric_complete_graph                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the overparameterized, qubit-specific ring ansatz with a permutation-symmetric    │
│                          │ block whose three rotation parameters are shared across all qubits. Because the 28 binary │
│                          │ features correspond to all qubit pairs, complete-graph CZ entanglement aligns the circuit │
│                          │ topology with the feature structure and avoids privileging an arbitrary ordering. The     │
│                          │ shared pre-mixing, phase, and post-mixing angles reduce the circuit parameter count from  │
│                          │ 146 to 20, improving parameter efficiency and regularization while retaining noncommuting │
│                          │ transformations around the diagonal feature map. This structure previously achieved       │
│                          │ substantially better validation accuracy, lower loss, a smaller generalization gap, and   │
│                          │ faster convergence.                                                                       │
