│ patch_name               │ symmetric_complete_graph                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the over-parameterized pair-specific block with a globally shared,                │
│                          │ permutation-symmetric block. Since the 28 binary features correspond to all qubit pairs   │
│                          │ and the readout averages Z over every qubit, complete-graph CZ mixing aligns the circuit  │
│                          │ inductive bias with both the feature representation and measurement symmetry. Sharing one │
│                          │ parameter across each local rotation layer reduces the model from 80 to 20 total          │
│                          │ parameters, improving regularization and parameter efficiency while eliminating the       │
│                          │ weakly motivated asymmetric CRZ bridge. Prior results indicate this structure             │
│                          │ substantially improves validation accuracy, loss, generalization, and convergence speed.  │
