│ patch_description        │ This block uses parameter-efficient, noncommuting mixing to complement the IsingZZ        │
│                          │ feature map. Independent RY rotations let each qubit adapt to its feature incidence,      │
│                          │ while parity-shared RZ parameters regularize the model and reduce the train-test gap. A   │
│                          │ CZ ring provides stable global connectivity, and four parametrized CRY gates across       │
│                          │ opposing qubits introduce directed, data-dependent mixing without excessive parameter     │
│                          │ growth. Reversing the direction of alternating CRY links avoids a single control-qubit    │
│                          │ bottleneck. The block uses only 14 unique parameters, making the six independently        │
│                          │ parameterized applications comparatively efficient and fast to optimize.                  │
