│ patch_name               │ symmetric_complete_graph                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the over-parameterized pair-specific block with the strongest                     │
│                          │ permutation-equivariant design from prior results. Sharing each rotation across all       │
│                          │ qubits reduces the circuit from 13 to 4 parameters per block and total parameters from 80 │
│                          │ to 26, improving regularization and parameter efficiency. Complete-graph CZ entanglement  │
│                          │ aligns the ansatz with all 28 pairwise feature channels, while one controlled phase adds  │
│                          │ limited symmetry-breaking expressivity. The final shared RY layer converts accumulated    │
│                          │ feature-dependent phases into the mean-Z measurement basis. Prior metrics indicate this   │
│                          │ structure raises validation accuracy to about 0.96, lowers validation loss to about 0.23, │
│                          │ and reduces the generalization gap.                                                       │
