│ patch_name               │ symmetric_complete_graph_bridge                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the overparameterized line ansatz with a strongly regularized, permutation-aware  │
│                          │ block. Sharing each rotation across all wires reduces the model from 24 to 4 parameters   │
│                          │ per block, lowering the total from 146 to 26 parameters while retaining independent       │
│                          │ copies across the six fixed blocks. Complete-graph CZ entanglement mirrors all 28         │
│                          │ pairwise feature channels, and a trainable CRZ on the 6–7 bridge adds adaptive phase      │
│                          │ coupling without materially increasing complexity. The final shared RY layer converts the │
│                          │ learned phase correlations into the mean-Z readout basis. This combines the strong        │
│                          │ validation behavior of symmetric complete-graph parents with the proposed localized 6–7   │
│                          │ trainable bridge.                                                                         │
