│ patch_name               │ symmetric_complete_graph                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the overparameterized pair-specific block with a permutation-symmetric,           │
│                          │ three-parameter block. Globally shared pre-RY, phase-RZ, and post-RY angles align with    │
│                          │ the mean-Z readout and regularize the six independent block copies. A fixed complete CZ   │
│                          │ graph mirrors all 28 pairwise feature channels, while removing the trainable CRZ avoids   │
│                          │ redundant phase capacity. This reduces the model from 13 to 3 parameters per block and    │
│                          │ from 80 to 20 total parameters, improving parameter efficiency and reducing overfitting   │
│                          │ while restoring the stronger full-connectivity inductive bias demonstrated by prior       │
│                          │ candidates.                                                                               │
