│ patch_description        │ Replace the overparameterized 24-parameter-per-block ring ansatz with a four-parameter    │
│                          │ symmetric block. Complete CZ pair coverage aligns the circuit connectivity with all 28    │
│                          │ IsingZZ feature channels, while two shared central CRZ bridges provide adaptive           │
│                          │ entanglement without sacrificing parameter efficiency. Globally shared pre/post rotations │
│                          │ regularize the six independent block copies and match the permutation-invariant mean-Z    │
│                          │ readout. A final RX mixer reuses the bridge parameter, adding a noncommuting              │
│                          │ phase-to-population conversion at zero parameter cost; this combines the stronger         │
│                          │ accuracy of the two-bridge parent with the faster dual-axis optimization behavior of the  │
│                          │ RX-mixer parent. The resulting model has 26 total parameters instead of 146.              │
