│ patch_name               │ shared_triple_crz_bridge                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the overparameterized local ring ansatz with the strongest prior symmetric        │
│                          │ complete-graph design, augmented by a third shared central CRZ bridge on wires [1, 6].    │
│                          │ Global parameter sharing aligns with the permutation-symmetric mean-Z readout and reduces │
│                          │ the model from 146 to 26 total parameters, improving parameter efficiency and             │
│                          │ regularization. The complete CZ graph mirrors all 28 pairwise feature channels, while     │
│                          │ three complementary CRZ bridges reuse one parameter to add adaptive phase interactions    │
│                          │ without increasing N_PARAMS. The final shared RY layer converts those learned phases into │
│                          │ Z populations. This targets the prior 0.95 score while testing the recommended extra      │
│                          │ bridge for higher accuracy or lower loss.                                                 │
